  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to question,\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/_0atlPd0xNFWe4Nv21YtL27zD-stVAdxmilFQ-sRn0Q.original.fullsize.png\"/>\nLet find slope of $A B, B C$ and $C A$\nSlope of $A B=\\frac{1-3}{1-(-2)}=\\frac{-2}{3}$\nSlope of $B C=\\frac{3-\\left(\\frac{5}{3}\\right)}{-2-0}=\\frac{-2}{3}$\nSlope of $C A=\\frac{\\frac{5}{3}-1}{0-1}=\\frac{-2}{3}$\nSince, slope of all lines are same, therefore, points are collinear.",
    "image": null
